    {
        "id": "c18c47bacbac6eeb",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "17d7519059560984",
        "g": "2107815757999873",
        "name": "Start (readme)",
        "info": "# Setting up your battery strategy flow\n\n## Setup\nName the `Link In node` in this start group exactly after the <select> option configured in your\nselect_input.house_battery_strategy\n\nconfigure select options in:\nhbc_control.yaml\n\n### example\n`house_battery_strategy:\n  name: House Battery Strategy\n  options:\n    - AcmE example`\n\nThe above creates a select option, allowing user to select 'AcmE example'\n\nWhen selected, battery control will search for a flow containing a Link In node\ncalled 'AcmE example' (case sensitive).",
        "x": 130,
        "y": 180,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "0712571b7dcc2a15",
        "type": "function",
        "z": "17d7519059560984",
        "g": "2107815757999873",
        "name": "Trace",
        "func": "// HBC+ 2026-11-15 (same as Self-consumption's Trace since 2026-10-13): was a change node with the JSONata expression\n//   [strategy.trace, {\"flow\": target, \"flow_settings\": advanced_settings, \"timestamp\": $now()}]\n// Same result in plain JavaScript (JSONata is slow and this runs on every tick).\nconst prev = RED.util.getMessageProperty(msg, 'strategy.trace');\nconst trace = prev === undefined || prev === null ? [] : (Array.isArray(prev) ? prev.slice() : [prev]);\nconst entry = { flow: msg.target };\nif (msg.advanced_settings !== undefined) entry.flow_settings = msg.advanced_settings;\nentry.timestamp = new Date().toISOString();\ntrace.push(entry);\nRED.util.setMessageProperty(msg, 'strategy.trace', trace, true);\nreturn msg;\n",
        "outputs": 1,
        "timeout": 0,
        "noerr": 0,
        "initialize": "",
        "finalize": "",
        "libs": [],
        "x": 110,
        "y": 220,
        "wires": [
            [
                "d31b8e8647339c0e"
            ]
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "47c0d76e5f88890f",
        "type": "link out",
        "z": "17d7519059560984",
        "g": "0d5a25185bd560da",
        "name": "Return",
        "mode": "return",
        "links": [],
        "x": 185,
        "y": 620,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "8bcb6192e1e3e470",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "17d7519059560984",
        "g": "0d5a25185bd560da",
        "name": "End (readme)",
        "info": "Should return a solution_array of battery objects\n\n## battery object format\n`{{id: string|number, mode: string, power: number}} battery solution`\n- id is an arbitrary battery ID\n- mode is \"stop\", \"charge\", \"discharge\" for Marstek\n- power in Watts\n\n### example array\nreturn this type of solution_array via msg.solutions\n` \nlet solution_array = [];\nsolution_array.push({id:\"M1\", mode: \"charge\", power: 100}); // per battery\nreturn {solutions: solution_array};\n` ",
        "x": 130,
        "y": 560,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "36bfa78c14881971",
        "type": "function",
        "z": "17d7519059560984",
        "g": "cb55caed48fda19c",
        "name": "Max power solution",
        "func": "// Logger, usage: log(this, \"\");\nconst log = global.get('logger');\nlog(this, \"Discharge at **max. power**\");\n\n// INPUT\nlet batteries = msg.batteries;\nlet solution_array = [];\n\n// HBC+ phase guard (2026-11-14), only when msg.phase_plus.mode === 'Enforce':\n// on a shared phase only the planner-active battery runs (others idle at 1 W, relay stays\n// engaged) and the total stays within the fuse room. Otherwise: every battery at max, as before.\nconst pp = msg.phase_plus;\nconst enforce = !!(pp && pp.mode === 'Enforce' && pp.phases);\nconst left = {};\nif (enforce) for (const [ph, e] of Object.entries(pp.phases)) left[ph] = Number(e.room && e.room.discharge) || 0;\n\n// build solution\nmsg.batteries.forEach(battery => {\n    let calculatedPower = Number(battery.discharging_max);\n\n    const ph = enforce ? pp.phase_of[battery.id] : null;\n    if (ph) {\n        const allowed = (pp.phases[ph].active && pp.phases[ph].active.discharge) || [];\n        if (!allowed.includes(battery.id)) {\n            calculatedPower = 1;\n            log(this, `Battery ${battery.id}: HBC+ phase standby on ${ph} (idle 1 W)`);\n        } else {\n            calculatedPower = Math.max(1, Math.min(calculatedPower, left[ph]));\n            left[ph] -= calculatedPower;\n            log(this, `Battery ${battery.id}: ${calculatedPower} W (HBC+ fuse room ${ph})`);\n        }\n    }\n\n    solution_array.push({\n        id: battery.id,\n        mode: \"discharge\",\n        power: calculatedPower\n    });\n\n});\n\n// return solution\nmsg.solutions = solution_array;\nreturn msg;\n",
        "outputs": 1,
        "timeout": 0,
        "noerr": 0,
        "initialize": "",
        "finalize": "",
        "libs": [],
        "x": 610,
        "y": 460,
        "wires": [
            [
                "dfb5b921e72ab3c3"
            ]
        ]
    },
