    {
        "id": "a9f483523fd25c63",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "17d7519059560984",
        "name": "📖 How this flow works - HBC+ v1.0 (open the Info sidebar)",
        "info": "# HBC+ Strategy Sell v1.0 - how this flow works\n\nPart of **HBC+ v1.0** (Home Battery Control Plus), with the phase guard for two batteries per phase. HBC+ settings live in `packages/hbc_phase_guard.yaml` and on the **Phases** view of the HBC+ dashboard.\n\nDischarges the batteries to the grid **until a goal is reached**, then hands over to the *goal reached* strategy.\n\n## Goal (`input_select.house_battery_strategy_sell_goal`)\n\n| Goal | Reached when |\n|---|---|\n| batteries are empty | usable energy is 0 kWh (all batteries at their min SoC) |\n| state of charge | the average SoC drops to `input_number.house_battery_strategy_sell_target_soc` |\n| energy reserve | usable energy drops to `input_number.house_battery_strategy_sell_target_energy` |\n| anything else | not recognised -> Full stop |\n\nWhen the goal is reached, the strategy in `input_select.house_battery_strategy_sell_goal_reached` runs (default *Charge PV*).\n\n## Power\n\n- **Export limit on** (`input_boolean.house_battery_control_has_power_limit_export`): *Regulated power* - Self-consumption is driven to grid export = the export limit, with charging disabled.\n- **No export limit**: *Max power solution* - every battery at its max discharge power.\n\n## HBC+ v1.0 - two batteries per phase\n\nThe phase rules only act when `input_select.house_battery_phase_guard_mode` is **Enforce**. On **Off** and **Monitor** this flow works without phase rules.\n\n- *Max power solution*: on a shared phase only the active battery (by default the one with the highest SoC) discharges, at min(its max, the phase's discharge room). Its partner idles at 1 W. The discharge room shrinks when PV is already exporting on that phase.\n- *Regulated power* goes through Self-consumption, which applies the same rules.\n",
        "x": 250,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
